    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Delayed puberty: a short course of ↓dose testosterone (boys) or estrogen (girls) = often started when delayed puberty and growth cause substantial psychosocial stress."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Girls: ↓dose 17β-estradiol (PO or transdermal patch) = the preferred initial tx; estrogen = ↑ over time until breakthrough bleed or 12–24 mo of tx, then combined estrogen + progesterone keeps norm monthly w.draw bleed; PO estrogen + progesterone, or transdermal estrogen + PO progesterone, are more physiological than OCPs."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
